WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.370
Marvel's Hulk might be the strongest there
is, but he's not invincible.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:09.400
The big green guy and his human alter ego,
Bruce Banner, have battled heroes and villains

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.509
alike since his debut in 1962.

00:00:12.509 --> 00:00:16.860
And while Hulk may be the strongest, it's
only natural that he's still taken a few big

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.050
losses along the way.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:21.570
Here are some of the more notable fights that
go in the Hulk's L column.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:25.910
But, just one warning to those who've given
the Hulk a decisive beatdown: he always comes

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.999
back angry — and you wouldn't like him when
he's angry.

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:29.999
Thor

00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:36.290
In 2001's Incredible Hulk Annual, Thor, fresh
off of a battle of his own, decides to help

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.110
local authorities stop the Hulk's rampage.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:43.150
The Asgardian equivalent of a sucker-punch
— a thunderbolt straight to Hulk's face

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:48.710
— gives Thor an early edge, but the brawl
continues across multiple dimensions before

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.710
a winner emerges.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:54.290
Ultimately, however, it's Thor's biology,
not his battle prowess, that puts him ahead.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:59.340
While the Hulk is distracted by local wildlife,
Bruce Banner takes control of the Hulk's body.

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:04.290
However, the otherworldly atmosphere doesn't
have enough oxygen for a regular human, and

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:07.860
Banner passes out, leaving Thor victorious.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:08.860
Deadpool

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.790
It's hard to believe, but in one of Deadpool's
very first solo appearances, he picked a one-on-one

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.180
fight with the Hulk.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.180
And won.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:21.830
In 1997’s Deadpool #4, Wade Wilson learns
that his healing factor is breaking down,

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.710
and if that goes, the cancer that plagues
his body will make a quick and fatal return.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.580
Even worse, there's only one cure: a sample
of the Hulk's gamma-irradiated blood.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.210
Tracking down the Hulk is easy.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.690
Getting a sample of his blood isn't.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:39.760
Deadpool's swords don't make much of a dent
in the Hulk's thick green hide, and Deadpool

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:42.420
doesn't stand a chance in a straight-up brawl.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.930
But Deadpool's not just crazy — he's also
smart.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:49.440
When the Hulk leaps straight towards him,
Deadpool points an old broken pipe right at

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:50.710
the charging beast.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:54.710
Hulk impales himself, and Deadpool collects
a blood sample from the monster's bleeding

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.920
wound before the Hulk can recover.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.470
Eventually, the Hulk frees himself by pulling
the pipe out of the ground, but not before

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:04.830
Deadpool makes an extremely speedy getaway.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:05.830
Juggernaut

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:10.700
Cain Marko, better known as the Juggernaut,
has super-strength and super-endurance.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:15.549
But his most notable power is that once he's
in motion he's literally unstoppable.

00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:21.689
That ability came in pretty handy in The Incredible
Hulk #402, when the Hulk took over a government

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:26.549
agency called the Pantheon and immediately
headed to South America on a peacekeeping

00:02:26.549 --> 00:02:27.549
mission.

00:02:27.549 --> 00:02:32.079
There, Hulk ran into a casually dressed Juggernaut,
who immediately launched an attack.

00:02:32.079 --> 00:02:36.779
Hulk spent most of the fight distracted — he
didn't recognize Marko in everyday clothes

00:02:36.779 --> 00:02:41.989
— and yet seemed to have the Juggernaut
put away when Marko sank in a pit of quicksand.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:45.450
But nothing can stop the Juggernaut, not even
Mother Nature.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.939
Juggernaut burst out of the trap, put Hulk
in a sleeper-hold, and went on to beat the

00:02:49.939 --> 00:02:52.480
stuffing out of his opponent.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.480
Batman

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.110
That's right: Batman went toe-to-toe with
the Hulk, and claimed victory in the process.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:03.609
It all happened in DC Special Series #27,
an intercompany crossover that came out in

00:03:03.609 --> 00:03:05.739
September of 1981.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.489
Using a false identity, Bruce Banner sneaks
into a job at Wayne Enterprises, which was

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:13.629
manufacturing a brand new gamma radiation
gun.

00:03:13.629 --> 00:03:17.349
Banner hoped the device could get rid of the
Hulk once and for all, but before he could

00:03:17.349 --> 00:03:19.200
find out, the Joker attacked.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.970
Bruce hulked out just as Batman arrived, and
it wasn't long before they were duking it

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:26.019
out in a Wayne Research laboratory.

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:29.489
That the two of them would get into a fight
isn't surprising.

00:03:29.489 --> 00:03:35.139
What is surprising is the simplicity of Batman's
plan: a pellet of sleeping gas and a well-timed

00:03:35.139 --> 00:03:37.620
kick to the gut, and the Hulk goes down.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.799
And that wouldn't be the last time the Hulk
faced off against a member of Marvel's distinguished

00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:43.579
competition...

00:03:43.579 --> 00:03:44.579
Superman

00:03:44.579 --> 00:03:50.510
In 1996, the DC and Marvel universes squared
off in a four-part miniseries appropriately

00:03:50.510 --> 00:03:52.680
called DC vs. Marvel.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.790
One of the series' best gimmicks was that
it gave fans the ability to vote on who would

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:59.029
win in each superpowered showdown.

00:03:59.029 --> 00:04:03.290
While the Marvel Universe ended up on top
once the dust cleared, when Superman beat

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:07.280
the Hulk at the polls, he laid the smack down
on the printed page as well.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.540
It's not even close.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.859
While the Hulk lands a few good punches, a
heat-vision barrage and a well-placed strike

00:04:12.859 --> 00:04:16.609
to the jaw is all that the Last Son of Krypton
needs to put him down.

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:18.799
The only silver lining for Hulk fans?

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:23.889
The version of the Hulk featured in DC vs.
Marvel had previously traded some of his strength

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:26.330
in order to keep Bruce Banner's intellect.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:28.250
But if the Hulk had been at full power?

00:04:28.250 --> 00:04:30.680
Maybe it would've been a different story...

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.680
Hawkeye

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.319
If the Hulk has a weakness, it's Bruce Banner.

00:04:34.319 --> 00:04:38.880
The easiest way to put down the jade giant
is to stop Banner before he transforms.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.740
That's how Hawkeye deals with the Hulk in
Marvel's mega-event series Civil War II.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:48.789
When a young man named Ulysses prophesies
a Hulk-fueled disaster, superheroes gather

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:52.889
on Bruce Banner's doorstep and ask the scientist
to turn himself in.

00:04:52.889 --> 00:04:57.080
Before Banner can comply, however, Hawkeye
— who claims that he saw Banner's eyes flash

00:04:57.080 --> 00:05:00.300
green — lets loose an arrow, killing Banner
instantly.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:04.889
But, for what it’s worth, Banner did ask
him to do it if he ever felt he might hurt

00:05:04.889 --> 00:05:06.319
innocent people.

00:05:06.319 --> 00:05:08.750
So...hooray for the good guys?

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:09.750
The Hulk

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:14.919
In the Future Imperfect storyline, the Hulk
takes on his own worst enemy — the Hulk.

00:05:14.919 --> 00:05:17.389
And as you might guess, it doesn't go so well.

00:05:17.389 --> 00:05:22.330
Set about 100 years in the future, Future
Imperfect explores a world where war has wiped

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.240
out heroes and villains alike.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:29.140
The Hulk, now calling himself the Maestro,
rules the world with an iron fist, thanks

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:34.050
to a combination of Bruce Banner's intelligence,
nuclear-powered strength, and a century's

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.790
worth of pent-up rage.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:40.390
Rebels use a time machine to bring the present-day
Hulk into the future, hoping that the strongest

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:43.419
one there is can stop a warlord who's even
stronger.

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:48.110
Unfortunately, the Maestro knows all of the
Hulk's moves and then some, and easily defeats

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.630
his younger counterpart, ultimately snapping
the Hulk's neck.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:56.330
The Hulk eventually recovers and confronts
the Maestro again, and while he still can't

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.599
physically defeat the despot, he does end
up winning.

00:05:59.599 --> 00:06:04.080
Using the same time machine that propelled
him into the future, Hulk sends the Maestro

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:07.560
back to the gamma explosion that created him
in the first place.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:12.250
The Maestro is incinerated at the exact same
time the Hulk is born, leading to a victory

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.620
for the good guys — and two decisive Hulk
beatdowns in one epic story.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:21.280
Now if that's not epic enough for you, strap
yourself in for the Hulk's most diabolical

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.490
foe yet.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:25.919
That's right, we're going to talk about the
time the Hulk was defeated by...

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:27.710
Puppies

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:28.710
Over the years, S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.770
has tangled with the Hulk numerous times,
and as one of the most important and technologically

00:06:33.770 --> 00:06:38.469
advanced peacekeeping agencies on the planet,
it only makes sense that they'd put that experience

00:06:38.469 --> 00:06:39.580
to good use.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.830
In 2013's The Indestructible Hulk Special,
S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:48.110
unleashed its latest, greatest, and cutest
anti-Hulk weapon: a crate crammed full of

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.110
puppies.

00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:52.040
See, while the Hulk might be a monster, he's
not heartless.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:56.580
The onslaught of adorable little furballs
eased the Green Goliath's nerves and forced

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:01.159
a transformation back into the Hulk's mild-mannered
alter-ego, Bruce Banner.

00:07:01.159 --> 00:07:03.650
Not very scientific, but it got the job done.

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.840
So the next time you're facing off against
a giant, green rage monster, don't forget

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:09.849
to bring a couple of cute doggos along.

00:07:09.849 --> 00:07:11.020
Thanks for watching!

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:13.919
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:13.919 --> 00:07:16.059
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love too!

